WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:01.970
I'll never forgive them...

00:33.840 --> 00:42.610
(Wanting you to just be near,
to feel your breath upon my ear)

00:42.650 --> 00:51.650
(Wishing you would call my name,
'Cause only you can light the flame)

00:51.690 --> 00:58.420
Constantly searching,
still can't find

01:01.030 --> 01:07.100
Ever illusive peace of mind

01:09.270 --> 01:17.840
Sometimes it's near,
but slips away

01:17.880 --> 01:24.480
And I'm faced with another day

01:25.690 --> 01:31.420
Of wanting you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:31.460 --> 01:35.760
...to just be near
('Cause only you can light the flame)

01:35.800 --> 01:40.240
Of wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:40.270 --> 01:44.670
...would call my name,
to feel your breath upon my ear

01:44.710 --> 01:49.200
Of wanting you... wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:49.250 --> 01:57.090
Call my name, 'cause only
you can light the flame

02:32.050 --> 02:34.210
Brother, it's me, Momosuke!

02:34.510 --> 02:35.920
I've returned from Kyoto!

02:38.180 --> 02:41.510
The master is out right now.

02:44.770 --> 02:45.640
I am...

02:45.720 --> 02:48.140
Momosuke-sama, right?

02:48.390 --> 02:50.140
Where is my brother?

02:50.520 --> 02:51.350
Momosuke!

02:51.900 --> 02:53.020
Is that you, Momosuke?

02:59.900 --> 03:01.070
I'm sorry I haven't kept in touch.

03:01.150 --> 03:02.780
Not at all. Thank you for coming.

03:08.870 --> 03:09.740
His name is Jihei.

03:10.080 --> 03:13.080
It's rather inconvenient living alone, but he helps me.

03:15.040 --> 03:16.960
This place hasn't changed...

03:17.590 --> 03:19.500
I was adopted before I was old enough to remember it,

03:19.630 --> 03:23.090
but the place seems strangely familiar.

03:24.220 --> 03:26.680
That just means you've gotten old.

03:26.890 --> 03:27.640
Not at all...

03:28.220 --> 03:31.510
I heard... you ran away from Ikomaya?

03:31.890 --> 03:33.010
I did not!

03:33.220 --> 03:38.270
I wanted to publish a book of 100 Stories,
so I left on a journey to collect strange stories and kaidan!

03:39.940 --> 03:40.980
Is that so?

03:41.060 --> 03:43.980
Knowing you, I'm sure you'll be
able to write something very interesting.

03:44.400 --> 03:47.740
More importantly, what did you
want to talk with me about, brother?

03:47.780 --> 03:49.530
Talk with you? What are you talking about?

03:50.450 --> 03:53.950
But... didn't you send a
letter all the way to Kyoto for me?

03:54.330 --> 03:55.280
A letter?

03:55.740 --> 03:57.240
I don't know anything about that.

03:57.500 --> 04:00.250
This is the first I've heard about you being in Kyoto, too.

04:04.670 --> 04:06.210
That's strange...

04:07.000 --> 04:08.210
I know the letter was right here...

04:08.590 --> 04:10.880
No, it may be for the best.

04:11.470 --> 04:11.880
What?

04:19.600 --> 04:21.720
A strange death?

04:22.310 --> 04:25.520
Yes, his name is Kijuurou Hamada,

04:25.770 --> 04:30.650
[Note: Sennin Doushin - A police force created by the Shogun to serve
as a border guard in Hachiouji, which lies on the outskirts of Edo.]

04:25.770 --> 04:28.270
He was a Sennin Doushin like me.

04:29.110 --> 04:30.650
There's a stone in his forehead?

04:30.940 --> 04:34.030
Even a sling couldn't produce this effect.

04:34.150 --> 04:35.490
Gunpowder, perhaps?

04:35.650 --> 04:39.860
No. Don't you think the stone is too round
to have come from something shattered by gunpowder?

04:40.370 --> 04:43.160
The stone... it's slightly scorched, isn't it?

04:45.410 --> 04:46.620
It's troubling me.

04:47.830 --> 04:51.290
If this is a murder, and I can't find the killer soon,

04:51.380 --> 04:55.590
it will bring disgrace to Hachiouji's Sennin Doushin,
which is under the government's direct supervision.

04:56.420 --> 04:58.880
Even government officials have it hard, I guess.

04:59.130 --> 05:02.340
I've managed to keep this a secret
until now, but not for much longer.

05:02.800 --> 05:03.720
And so...

05:05.010 --> 05:07.470
Have you ever heard of a story like this?

05:11.310 --> 05:13.520
A flying squirrel, perhaps?

05:13.980 --> 05:15.020
A flying squirrel?

05:15.650 --> 05:20.280
You mean the rat-like creature that flies from tree to tree?

05:21.360 --> 05:24.490
Flying squirrels that have lived for a
very long time are called "Nobusuma".

05:25.070 --> 05:30.200
Nobusuma are said to cling to people's
faces, suffocate them, and drink their blood.

05:31.290 --> 05:37.420
It is said that a badger or tanuki called
"Nodeppou" launches the Nobusuma at people.

05:37.790 --> 05:41.750
Nodeppou would blow the
Nobusuma towards travelers on mountain paths.

05:42.340 --> 05:43.750
Nodeppou?

05:44.760 --> 05:48.970
But Kijuurou was neither suffocated
nor was his blood sucked out of him.

05:49.720 --> 05:57.390
It is also said that there are supernatural
entities, such as tengu, that attack people with slingshots.

05:59.100 --> 06:01.770
If he was attacked by a youkai,
guess there is nothing we can do.

06:02.980 --> 06:04.810
Who would believe such nonsense?

06:05.190 --> 06:06.650
H-However...!

06:07.110 --> 06:11.610
Tagami-sama, it is also possible that
there is someone lurking in the Iriyama pass.

06:14.450 --> 06:16.660
All right. Tomorrow, we search the pass!

06:16.950 --> 06:21.910
Wait! If it really is a youkai, we are powerless against it!

06:22.040 --> 06:25.120
Matashirou! Have you fallen prey to fear?

06:27.290 --> 06:28.000
No.

06:28.460 --> 06:31.670
But if a Nodeppou is really there...

06:32.300 --> 06:34.010
Is there a way to protect ourselves from it?

06:34.420 --> 06:36.630
It's said that, to protect yourself from Nobusuma,

06:36.880 --> 06:39.930
you must conceal cockleburs in your bosom.

06:40.430 --> 06:41.720
Cockleburs, eh?

06:42.640 --> 06:44.930
Then it's decided; we will search the pass tomorrow.

06:46.140 --> 06:47.270
Don't run away.

06:54.480 --> 06:55.980
Still a lightweight?

06:56.650 --> 07:00.490
If you don't drink some sake,
nobody will tell you any interesting stories.

07:01.910 --> 07:05.330
But drinking sake gives me a huge headache...

07:06.490 --> 07:08.410
If you can overcome that, it will be fun.

07:08.910 --> 07:09.950
I wonder if that is so.

07:10.250 --> 07:11.000
Drink up.

07:18.630 --> 07:21.800
Your face hasn't changed a bit since you were a baby.

07:21.800 --> 07:22.840
Brother...

07:23.220 --> 07:25.550
Shall I bring you some snacks to go with the sake?

07:25.840 --> 07:26.970
Yes, thanks.

07:27.430 --> 07:29.970
Drinking has been fun ever since Jihei came.

07:32.180 --> 07:32.770
Who could that be?

07:33.180 --> 07:34.230
Yamaoka-dono?

07:34.560 --> 07:36.230
Are you there, Yamaoko-dono?

07:36.980 --> 07:37.770
Matashirou?

07:39.190 --> 07:40.690
What brings you here at this hour?

07:42.150 --> 07:46.070
Actually... it wasn't a youkai that killed Kijuurou.

07:46.450 --> 07:47.420
What?

07:47.880 --> 07:48.830
I...

07:48.910 --> 07:51.030
I know everything.

07:53.790 --> 07:56.580
It's true that it's called
"Nodeppou", just like the mononoke.

07:57.040 --> 08:02.290
But that's... that's... a gun that fires rocks!

08:02.880 --> 08:04.500
A gun that fires rocks, you say?

08:05.000 --> 08:06.050
Such a thing exists?

08:08.380 --> 08:10.420
There is a stone-using crossbow that has been passed down

08:10.420 --> 08:12.970
since ancient times among
the pirates of the Seto Inland Sea.

08:13.390 --> 08:16.970
Their boss, Shimazou, improved
its design and made the Nodeppou.

08:17.260 --> 08:18.260
What?

08:18.390 --> 08:19.470
How do you know this?

08:19.970 --> 08:27.190
That's because... I once was a
part of Boss Shimazou's pirate gang.

08:34.650 --> 08:36.240
You have betrayed me...

08:37.070 --> 08:41.870
Heh, you thought you could
just retire by yourself and enjoy life?

08:42.240 --> 08:44.410
The Nodeppou... is that what you're after?

08:44.660 --> 08:46.540
If you know that, there's not much more to talk about.

08:46.830 --> 08:48.790
Now, out with it.

08:48.880 --> 08:50.130
Where are you hiding it?

08:50.330 --> 08:52.920
There's no way I'll hand it over to people like you!

08:53.800 --> 08:55.960
I wonder how long you'll be able to keep that attitude up.

09:01.680 --> 09:02.260
Otami!

09:02.800 --> 09:06.850
Don't you treasure the life of your cute granddaughter?

09:09.180 --> 09:10.100
Otami!

09:12.100 --> 09:16.730
If I give them that gun,
they'll use it against many innocent people...

09:16.900 --> 09:20.280
Shut up! If you don't hurry, we'll kill her!

09:23.070 --> 09:26.240
I-I'm sorry, Otami!

09:26.950 --> 09:27.950
Why, you...

09:27.990 --> 09:29.280
Th-This is bad!

09:38.420 --> 09:39.790
Grand... father...

09:45.840 --> 09:49.970
Otami!

09:52.890 --> 09:56.980
I... I just did as my brother asked.

09:57.640 --> 09:59.020
I didn't want it to end up like that...

09:59.270 --> 10:00.230
Where is Shimazou now?

10:00.440 --> 10:01.270
Dead.

10:01.860 --> 10:02.770
And his henchmen?

10:02.980 --> 10:04.720
They too are all...

10:05.420 --> 10:07.190
Wh-What should I do?

10:08.700 --> 10:10.950
Tell this to Tagami-sama tomorrow.

10:13.370 --> 10:15.450
I-I didn't do anything wrong!

10:16.370 --> 10:17.240
Matashirou!

10:43.730 --> 10:45.390
Save me!

11:11.810 --> 11:14.020
Matashirou was in a band of robbers, you say?

11:14.430 --> 11:14.890
Yes.

11:15.640 --> 11:17.310
He told me himself last night.

11:17.560 --> 11:19.560
Are you sure he hadn't drunk too much or something?

11:19.650 --> 11:21.110
No, he didnt seem like he had at all.

11:21.820 --> 11:23.110
Where is he now?

11:23.360 --> 11:25.440
He ran out of my house... and I haven't seen him since.

11:27.990 --> 11:30.110
Do you think he could've been playing a big trick on you?

11:30.570 --> 11:32.120
I hope that was the case...

11:36.750 --> 11:38.540
Here is your cocklebur. Put this around your neck.

11:43.920 --> 11:46.590
Are you ready? We leave now!

11:49.380 --> 11:51.550
Jihei-san? Jihei-san?

12:06.560 --> 12:08.310
Boss!

12:08.480 --> 12:10.230
Ji-Jihei?

12:10.480 --> 12:11.610
I'm done for.

12:11.650 --> 12:13.320
Wh-Who did this?

12:13.530 --> 12:16.070
More importantly, t-take this...

12:17.860 --> 12:24.410
Listen, you must protect this no
matter what... and then... I wish that you... my...

12:32.250 --> 12:34.340
Boss!

12:37.760 --> 12:38.670
It's Jihei-san!

13:07.700 --> 13:08.410
What's th'is?

13:41.350 --> 13:44.690
It was Nobusuma... Nobusuma...

14:07.000 --> 14:08.170
That's my brother's!

14:10.510 --> 14:11.760
I'm sorry, where is my brother?!

14:12.010 --> 14:12.960
Where is Yamaoka?

14:17.390 --> 14:18.220
Brother...

14:27.350 --> 14:29.730
This is your end...

14:34.030 --> 14:35.900
Otami!

14:38.400 --> 14:42.030
You... How dare you!

14:58.460 --> 14:59.710
There's no way around it...

14:59.880 --> 15:01.970
We'll have to make with just his money.

15:12.480 --> 15:14.020
I won't forgive you...

15:20.820 --> 15:21.610
Brother!

15:42.000 --> 15:44.290
It's not... Jihei-san?

15:44.460 --> 15:46.250
Somebody! Is somebody here?

15:46.630 --> 15:47.090
Brother!

15:51.300 --> 15:53.800
Brother, are you all right?

15:53.930 --> 15:56.930
Momosuke, it was just as you said.

15:57.890 --> 15:59.470
It wasn't some kind of stone-using rifle...

16:00.890 --> 16:03.020
It was the doing of an ayakashi!

16:04.600 --> 16:07.810
Did Tagami-sama give his
own life to avenge Kijuurou-dono?

16:09.030 --> 16:11.650
No, this is Mataichi-san's group's doing...

16:12.700 --> 16:13.400
Brother!

16:14.070 --> 16:16.320
Eh, it's nothing serious.

16:16.950 --> 16:19.120
I was attacked by Nobusuma, so...

16:20.240 --> 16:21.080
This is...

16:21.410 --> 16:23.290
Jihei made it for me.

16:24.120 --> 16:26.830
I was saved by what you told me.

16:31.380 --> 16:33.460
Some type of numbing medicine?

16:36.510 --> 16:37.340
What was that?

16:38.010 --> 16:39.630
Wait here!

16:48.350 --> 16:50.640
This isn't the doing of Nobusuma.

16:50.810 --> 16:52.100
It's Mataichi-san's group!

16:52.350 --> 16:54.110
They're doing it!

16:57.400 --> 16:58.230
You're...

16:59.320 --> 17:02.070
Ah, you got me...

17:02.160 --> 17:02.990
Nagamimi-san?

17:03.360 --> 17:05.450
Wh-What's with your body?

17:05.820 --> 17:07.200
Did you forget?

17:11.290 --> 17:13.620
So, you're behind this, after all.

17:13.920 --> 17:15.080
That's right.

17:15.120 --> 17:17.290
Then, the letter I got in Kyoto was from you?

17:17.840 --> 17:20.710
What? I don't know anything about a letter.

17:21.000 --> 17:22.380
What?! But...

17:22.510 --> 17:24.130
I don't know anything about it.

17:24.220 --> 17:28.090
In any case, if your brother is important
to you, take him and get the hell out of here.

17:28.340 --> 17:29.340
What do you mean?

17:29.550 --> 17:36.600
[Note: Onnen: Hatred so intense that it acquires
a will of its own and becomes a ghost of sorts.]

17:29.550 --> 17:35.730
Our plan went well enough,
but Jihei's body has been possessed by an onnen.

17:35.730 --> 17:36.600
What did you say?

17:39.150 --> 17:44.730
Whether it's the onnen of Shimazou or of
the people killed by the Nodeppou, I don't know.

17:46.150 --> 17:48.240
Onnen are troublesome things, you see.

17:48.450 --> 17:52.240
They were originally people,
but they have no humanity left in them!

17:52.490 --> 17:54.570
Hatred, hatred, hatred.

17:54.740 --> 17:56.200
That's all that is left of them.

17:57.500 --> 18:01.910
By now, all he wants to do is kill more
people and take their hatred into himself.

18:02.580 --> 18:06.670
Well, in other words, the weapon itself is an ayakashi.

18:07.000 --> 18:08.210
Where's Jihei-san?

18:08.250 --> 18:09.670
He headed for the village.

18:09.710 --> 18:13.380
What?! But the village is having a festival tonight!

18:13.380 --> 18:16.590
That's why I said to get the hell out of here.

18:16.800 --> 18:18.850
That's terrible! I have to stop him!

18:19.470 --> 18:21.720
So do you! Come on!

18:20.720 --> 18:23.220
Hey, se-sensei! But...

18:25.980 --> 18:28.810
He's always such an upright person...

18:28.810 --> 18:29.940
Jeez...

18:50.830 --> 18:52.250
Please, stop!

18:53.170 --> 18:53.960
Out of the way.

18:54.250 --> 18:56.380
Jihei-san, no, Shimazou-san!

18:56.840 --> 18:59.130
Your revenge should be over already!

19:00.090 --> 19:01.340
Shimazou-san!

19:14.270 --> 19:16.860
Sh-Shimazou-san! No!

19:17.020 --> 19:18.150
Please, stop!

19:20.030 --> 19:20.480
Kill.

19:21.820 --> 19:23.320
Shimazou-san!

19:28.910 --> 19:29.870
Grandpa!

19:30.790 --> 19:31.450
Otami?

19:31.540 --> 19:32.910
Grandpa, please!

19:34.830 --> 19:36.080
Stop!

19:36.160 --> 19:39.120
Kill.

19:40.880 --> 19:42.380
Like you killed us..

19:44.960 --> 19:47.090
Everyone is suffering!

19:47.670 --> 19:49.340
They were killed and are suffering!

19:49.800 --> 19:51.590
For all this time, we've been suffering...

19:56.970 --> 19:59.640
Wh-What happened to him, all of a sudden?

20:00.810 --> 20:03.230
I remember... Grandfather...

20:03.900 --> 20:06.570
A long time ago, we went to
a festival together, remember?

20:07.320 --> 20:11.740
You were so kind back then...
You never robbed the poor...

20:12.740 --> 20:14.280
Be that person again!

20:41.260 --> 20:43.310
What just... happened?

20:44.720 --> 20:48.850
Shimazou-san's soul defeated the Nodeppou's hatred.

20:48.940 --> 20:50.020
Mataichi-san!

20:50.520 --> 20:54.400
This time, there was no need for me to do my job.

20:55.440 --> 20:58.740
Shimazou-san was one heck of a guy.

20:59.240 --> 21:03.950
Even in death, he held to his
convictions and overcame the Nodeppou's onnen.

21:13.880 --> 21:16.080
The deed is done.

21:18.960 --> 21:21.800
It's quite bright down there, isn't it?

21:23.090 --> 21:25.090
The bright world of life...

21:25.590 --> 21:27.340
The dark world of death...

21:27.850 --> 21:33.140
In truth, the border between
the two realms is as thin as paper.

21:33.560 --> 21:36.730
We're the ones who live between the two.

21:38.610 --> 21:41.440
Do you mean to say that you live in a different world?

21:41.520 --> 21:42.270
Sensei!

21:43.820 --> 21:45.490
This place is too bright for us.

21:45.690 --> 21:47.820
I'll leave the rest to you.

21:58.330 --> 21:59.370
Where am I...?

22:00.290 --> 22:01.540
Let's go home.

22:15.580 --> 22:21.670
Wind chimes whisper
soft and sweet

22:23.020 --> 22:29.110
Though there's not
a hint of a breeze

22:30.090 --> 22:35.860
Moonlight dancing
on the garden walk

22:35.900 --> 22:42.530
As it gently drifts
through the trees

22:43.900 --> 22:49.840
Romance takes flight
on this perfect night

22:49.880 --> 22:56.540
While all of the world
lays sleeping

22:57.380 --> 23:06.850
Find us here as we feel
the moment of love

23:08.160 --> 23:11.360
Draw near

23:11.630 --> 23:18.630
Dream, sleep,
with your hand in mine

23:18.670 --> 23:24.610
Underneath a blanket of stars

23:26.780 --> 23:32.050
Song birds singing
in a distant glade

23:32.090 --> 23:40.720
As we share
the warmth of the dawn

23:50.600 --> 23:56.270
Evil and ambition scatter into the darkness.
All that remains is a dubious rumor among the townsfolk.

23:57.900 --> 24:02.730
There is a rumor that the decapitated
Giemon has revived for the third time.

24:03.190 --> 24:05.820
That which lurks in the shadows is Ogin's hatred.

24:07.650 --> 24:11.820
On the next Kyougoku Natsuhiko's Rumors: 100 Stories,

24:11.990 --> 24:12.780
Kowai.

24:13.330 --> 24:15.450
The deed is done.
